{"abstract":"As software grows in size and complexity, organizations increasingly apply tools to automatically assess software quality of information systems during development and maintenance. Software quality assessment tools (SWQAT) promise fast and actionable insights into the technical state of software through various quality characteristics, such as maintainability, reliability, or security. These tools have been used to support a wide variety of IT project management decisions related to system development, contract negotiations, project terminations, and even settling legal disputes between suppliers and clients. However, despite their rising importance, questions regarding how they function and how reliable they are to support decision-making have so far escaped scholarly attention. This paper conducts an evaluation of widely used SWQATs and analyzes how they rate the quality of software systems of varying sizes, functionalities, and programming languages. Our results reveal five key challenges for using SWQATs in IT projects. To address these challenges, we propose a design for tailorable SWQATs that allows for more conscious and prudent software quality assessments that better reflect the socio-technical aspect of software systems and the context-specific nature of software quality.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730195"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Project control and monitoring","Software quality","information systems management tools","software quality assessment tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tools for monitoring software quality in information systems development and maintenance five key challenges and a design proposal","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12821/ijispm120102","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730195","identifier":[{"id":"85189794450","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ce6096be-7169-4b94-9540-075b4aa62859"],"keyword":["information systems management tools","project control and monitoring","software quality","software quality assessment tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F909E08E82E61B2CA6ACD19E2EA7398E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103580697/ijispm-120102.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12821/ijispm120102","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"6b81fcf4-173e-4e8b-86d6-2c9e7b4320c6","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-ce6096be-7169-4b94-9540-075b4aa62859"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tools for monitoring software quality in information systems development and maintenance: five key challenges and a design proposal","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730195","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Interpreted programming languages, like Python, are amongst the most popular programming languages. This, combined with high developer eﬃciency leads to many web-application backends and web-services that are written in Python. While it is known that that interpreted languages like Python are way less energy eﬃcient compared to compiled languages like C++, Rust, etc., little is known about the energy eﬃciency of various versions of Python interpreters. In this paper, we study via a controlled lab experiment the energy consumption of various versions of the Python interpreter CPython when running a server-side rendered web-application. Our results indicate that currently the most energy eﬃcient version is CPython 3.12. Energy consumption of CPython 3.12 can drop by more than 8% compared to previous versions.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759391"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CPython","Energy consumptionython","Software Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the energy consumption of cpython","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu.dk/~ropf/blog/assets/pfeiffer_quatic2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759391","identifier":[{"id":"85204620883","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1f082f42-0db5-4822-83fe-eac234484fcc"],"keyword":["CPython","Energy consumptionython.","Software engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-38893205B5FCB42A647A0A8BC2B5EA4F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu.dk/~ropf/blog/assets/pfeiffer_quatic2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-70245-7_14","eisbn":["9783031702457"],"isbn":["9783031702440"],"pages":"194-209","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"17th International Conference on the Quality of Information and Communications Technology, QUATIC 2024, Pisa, Italy, September 11–13, 2024, Proceedings","title":"Quality of Information and Communications Technology","volume":"2178"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204620883"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1f082f42-0db5-4822-83fe-eac234484fcc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the Energy Consumption of CPython","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759391","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present the course “DevOps, Software Evolution, and Software Maintenance” that we developed and teach at IT University of Copenhagen. It differs from similar courses in that it focuses student project work on maintenance and evolution of a live software system.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Lungu, Mircea","Tell, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712505"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer Science Education","Education","Educational courses","Maintenance engineering","Monitoring","Production","Software Engineering","Training"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"live is life teaching software engineering on live systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MS.2023.3311376","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712505","identifier":[{"id":"85171528508","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2ae02a19-1699-4e52-8179-3d7f53e300f7"],"keyword":["Computer science education","Education","Educational courses","Maintenance engineering","Monitoring","Production","Software engineering","Training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD054F4A3EE6E788EA4524747CDCD46F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102402128/SWSI-2023-02-0022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MS.2023.3311376","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":[