enpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3524842.3528004","pages":"388-392","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"MSR '22: Proceedings of the 19th International Conference on Mining Software Repositories"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134077378"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1b98b062-fa33-425c-8d0a-bbef3e705117"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DaSEA – A Dataset for Software Ecosystem Analysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381679","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Together with many success stories, promises such as the increase in production speed and the improvement in stakeholders' collaboration have contributed to making agile a transformation in the software industry in which many companies want to take part. However, driven either by a natural and expected evolution or by contextual factors that challenge the adoption of agile methods as prescribed by their creator(s), software processes in practice mutate into hybrids over time. Are these still agile? In this article, we investigate the question: what makes a software development method agile? We present an empirical study grounded in a large-scale international survey that aims to identify software development methods and practices that improve or tame agility. Based on 556 data points, we analyze the perceived degree of agility in the implementation of standard project disciplines and its relation to used development methods and practices. Our findings suggest that only a small number of participants operate their projects in a purely traditional or agile manner (under 15 percent). That said, most project disciplines and most practices show a clear trend towards increasing degrees of agility. Compared to the methods used to develop software, the selection of practices has a stronger effect on the degree of agility of a given discipline. Finally, there are no methods or practices that explicitly guarantee or prevent agility. We conclude that agility cannot be defined solely at the process level. Additional factors need to be taken into account when trying to implement or improve agility in a software company. Finally, we discuss the field of software process-related research in the light of our findings and present a roadmap for future research.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Kuhrmann, Marco","Tell, Paolo","Hebig, Regina","Klunder, Jil Ann Christin","Munch, Jurgen","Linssen, Oliver","Pfahl, Dietmar","Felderer, Michael","Prause, Christian","Macdonell, Steve","Nakatumba-Nabende, Joyce","Raffo, David","Beecham, Sarah","Tuzun, Eray","Lopez, Gustavo","Paez, Nicolas","Fontdevila, Diego","Licorish, Sherlock","Kupper, Steffen","Ruhe, Guenther","Knauss, Eric","Ozcan-Top, Ozden","Clarke, Paul","Mc Caffery, Fergal Hugh","Genero, Marcela","Vizcaino, Aurora","Piattini, Mario","Kalinowski, Marcos","Conte, Tayana","Prikladnicki, Rafael","Krusche, Stephan","Coskuncay, Ahmet","Scott, Ezequiel","Calefato, Fabio","Pimonova, Svetlana","Pfeiffer, Rolf Helge","Schultz, Ulrik Pagh","Heldal, Rogardt","Fazal-Baqaie, Masud","Anslow, Craig","Nayebi, Maleknaz","Schneider, Kurt","Sauer, Stefan","Winkler, Dietmar","Biffl, Stefan","Bastarrica, Cecilia","Richardson, Ita"],"cuid":["S02-095.45-038398"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Schultz, Ulrik Pagh"],"country":["Argentina","Austria","Brazil","Canada","Chile","Costa Rica","Estonia","Germany","Ireland","Italy","New Zealand","Norway","Russia","Spain","Sweden","Turkey","Uganda","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ataturk University","Ataturk University School of Medicine","Bilkent University","Chalmers University of Technology","Clausthal University of Technology","Dublin City University","Dundalk Institute of Technology","Ecole Polytechnique de Montreal","FOM University of Applied Sciences","FOM die Hochschule für Berufstätige","Federal University of Amazonas","Fraunhofer Institute for Mechatronic Design","German Aerospace Center","Hochschule Reutlingen","Institut für Anorganische Chemie","Leibniz University Hannover","Leibniz Universität Hannover","Lero","Lero - The Irish Software Engineering Research Centre","Makerere University","Makerere University School of Public Health","Middle East Technical University",