owskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"148-163","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"8569"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84958527577"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-07fc1a13-c567-423d-8d8e-d6044d2a0f3a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Language-Independent Traceability with Lässig","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381377","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Non-trivial software systems integrate many artifacts expressed in multiple modeling and program- ming languages. However, even though these artifacts heavily depend on each other, existing development envi- ronments do not sufficiently support handling relations between artifacts in different languages. By means of a literature survey, tool prototyping and experiments we study the design space of multi-language development environments (MLDEs)—tools that consider the cross-language relations as first artifacts. We ask: what is the state of the art in the MLDE space? What are the design choices and challenges faced by tool builders? To what extent MLDEs are desired by users, and for what support features? Our main conclusions are that (a) cross-language re- lations are ubiquitous and troublesome in multi-language systems, (b) users highly appreciated cross-language sup- port mechanisms of MLDEs and (c) generic MLDEs clearly enhance the state of the art in tooling for lan- guage integration. The technical artifacts resulting from this study include a feature model of the MLDE do- main, a data set of harvested cross-language relations in a case study system (JTrac) and two MLDEs, TexMo and Coral, that implement two radically different choices in the design space.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381628"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross language relations","Multi language development environment","Multi modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the design space of multi language development environments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10270-013-0376-y","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381628","identifier":[{"id":"84922337844","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-17d16f14-581c-463c-a0b8-a73ca52e9101"],"keyword":["Cross-language relations","Multi-language development environment","Multi-modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7400D0706F712C8D8442F66C91A1054D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10270-013-0376-y","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf-Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","name_org":"Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10270-013-0376-y","issn":["16191366","16191374"],"issn_org":["16191366"],"journal":"Software and Systems Modeling","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Software and Systems Modeling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84922337844"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-17d16f14-581c-463c-a0b8-a73ca52e9101"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Design Space of Multi-Language Development Environments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381628","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Software ecosystems are increasingly popular for their economic, strategic, and technical advantages. Application platforms such as Android or iOS allow users to highly customize a system by selecting desired functionality from a large variety of assets. This customization is achieved using variability mechanisms. Variability mechanisms are well-researched in the context of software product lines. Although software ecosystems are often seen as conceptual successors, the technology that sustains their success and growth is much less understood. Our objective is to improve empirical understanding of variability mechanisms used in successful software ecosystems. We analyze five ecosystems, ranging from the Linux kernel through Eclipse to Android. A qualitative analysis identifies and characterizes variability mechanisms together with their organizational context. This analysis leads to a conceptual framework that unifies ecosystem-specific aspects using a common terminology. A quantitative analysis investigates scales, growth rates, and—most importantly—dependency structures of the ecosystems. In all the studied ecosystems, we identify rich dependency languages and variability descriptions that declare many direct and indirect dependencies. Indirect dependencies to abstract capabilities, as opposed to concrete variability units, are used predominantly in fast-growing ecosystems. We also find that variability models—while providing system-wide abstractions over code—work best in centralized variability management and are, thus, absent in ecosystems with large free markets. These latter ecosystems tend to emphasize maintaining capabilities and common vocabularies, dynamic discovery, and binding with strong encapsulation of contributions, together with uniform distribution channels. The use of specialized mechanisms in software ecosystems with large free markets, as opposed to software product lines, calls for recognition of a new discipline—variability encouragement.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Berger, Thorsten","Pfeiffer, Helge","Tartler, Reinhard","Dienst, Steffen","Czarnecki, Krzysztof","Wasowski, Andrzej","She, Steven"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383265"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Empirical Software Engineering","Mining Software Repositories","Software ecosystems","Software product lines","Variability Management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variability mechanisms in software ecosystems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84905441720","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383265","identifier":[{"id":"84905441720","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8821316e-8def-4fb8-aa7f-0c0562e55e62"],"keyword":["Empirical software engineering","Mining software repositories","Software ecosystems","Software product lines","Variability management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-06FFB4BDDA71C0649A806CD544F57270"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","name":"Berger, Thorsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf-Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","name_org":"Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Reinhard","key":"tartlerpau","last":"Tartler","name":"Tartler, Reinhard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dienstpau","last":"Dienst","name":"Dienst, Steffen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Krzysztof","key":"czarneckipau","last":"Czarnecki","name":"Czarnecki, Krzysztof","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven","key":"shepau","last":"She","name":"She, Steven","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09505849","18736025"],"issn_org":["09505849"],"issue":"11","journal":"Information and Software Technology","pages":"1520-1535","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information and Software Technology","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905441720"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8821316e-8def-4fb8-aa7f-0c0562e55e62"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Variability mechanisms in software ecosystems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383265","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Non-trivial software systems are constructed out of many artifacts expressed in multiple modeling and programming languages, describing different system aspects on different levels of abstraction. I call such systems multi-language software systems. Even though artifacts constituting multi-language software systems are heavily interrelated, existing development environments do not sufficiently support developers in development of such systems. In particular, handling relations between heterogeneous artifacts is not supported at development time. This thesis (a) studies the characteristics of contemporary multi-language software systems, (b) it investigates features needed in software development tools and environments to support or enhance multi-language software system development, and (c) it establishes required knowledge and building blocks for creation of multi-language development environments. I address these research goals by applying tool prototyping, technical experiments, user experiments, surveys, and literature survey as ethodological tools. The main results of this thesis are (a) a taxonomy for construction, comparison, and characterization of multi-language development environments (b) the identification of navigation, static checking, visualization and refactoring of cross-language relations as four elementary cross-language support echanisms, (c) the experimental evaluation of multi-language software system development with support of cross-language support mechanisms, (d) the characterization of two industrial strength open-source systems as multi-language software systems by technical experiments, (e) a characterization of the state-of-the-art in multi-language software system development and in multi-language development environments, and lastly (f) a set of open-source prototype tools, which implement different language representations and relation models and they implement different facets of multi-language development environments. My main conclusions are (a) contemporary software systems are indeed multilanguage software systems, (b) relations between heterogeneous development artifacts are ubiquitous and troublesome in multi-language software systems; they pose a real problem to development and evolution of multi-language software systems, (c) users highly appreciated cross-language support mechanisms of multi-language development environments, (d) generic MLDEs clearly enhance the state of the art in tooling for language integration, and (e) multilanguage development environments can be constructed by cautiously deciding on a language representation for heterogeneous development artifacts, a model for relations between heterogeneous development artifacts, and considering typical properties of heterogeneous development artifact relations.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382750"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi language development enviroments design space models prototypes experiences","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109063304/phd_thesis_print.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382750","ids":["itu-62ae8682-8ba1-4d65-8d88-62e55d0d365b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-56DBBBE6056AA5631FC095CA1D34EA23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109063304/phd_thesis_print.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf-Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","name_org":"Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779492905"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"95","pages":"247","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-62ae8682-8ba1-4d65-8d88-62e55d0d365b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-language Development Enviroments : Design Space, Models, Prototypes, Experiences","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382750","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Multiple system atrophy (MSA) is a fatal and still poorly understood degenerative movement disorder that is characterised by autonomic failure, cerebellar ataxia, and parkinsonism in various combinations. Here we present the final analysis of a prospective multicentre study by the European MSA Study Group to investigate the natural history of MSA.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Wenning, Gregor K","Geser, Felix","Krismer, Florian","Seppi, Klaus","Duerr, Susanne","Boesch, Sylvia","Köllensperger, Martin","Goebel, Georg","Pfeiffer, Karl P","Barone, Paolo","Pellecchia, Maria Teresa","Quinn, Niall P","Koukouni, Vasiliki","Fowler, Clare J","Schrag, Anette","Mathias, Christopher J","Giladi, Nir","Gurevich, Tanya","Dupont, Erik","Østergaard, Karen","Nilsson, Christer F","Widner, Håkan","Oertel, Wolfgang","Eggert, Karla Maria","Albanese, Alberto","Del Sorbo, Francesca","Tolosa, Eduardo","Cardozo, Adriana","Deuschl, Günther","Hellriegel, Helge","Klockgether, Thomas","Dodel, Richard","Sampaio, Cristina","Coelho, Miguel","Djaldetti, Ruth","Melamed, Eldad","Gasser, Thomas","Kamm, Christoph","Meco, Giuseppe","Colosimo, Carlo","Rascol, Olivier","Meissner, Wassilios G","Tison, François","Poewe, Werner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-207226"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["European Multiple System Atrophy Study Group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the natural history of multiple system atrophy a prospective european cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1474-4422(12)70327-7","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-207226","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3581815","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84876332892"