00-207226","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Contemporary software systems contain a large number of artifacts expressed in multiple languages, ranging from domain-specific languages to general purpose languages. These artifacts are interrelated to form software systems. Existing development environments insufficiently support handling relations between artifacts in multiple languages. This paper presents a taxonomy for multi-language development environments, organized according to language representation, representation of relations between languages, and types of these relations. Additionally, we present TexMo, a prototype of a multi-language development environment, which uses an explicit relation model and implements visualization, static checking, navigation, and refactoring of cross-language relations. We evaluate TexMo by applying it to development of a web-application, JTrac, and provide preliminary evidence of its feasibility by running user tests and interviews.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383506"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross language relations","Development environments","Multi language development","Software artifacts","Static checking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"texmo a multi language development environment","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-31491-9_15","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383506","identifier":[{"id":"84864059931","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-984a53cf-998d-42f1-9b30-ca6bdbf51973"],"keyword":["Cross-language relations","Development environments","Multi-language development","Software artifacts","Static checking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D3ECFEF58C721599FBAEE6892C3810F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-31491-9_15","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf-Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","name_org":"Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-31491-9_15","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"178-193","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7349"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864059931"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-984a53cf-998d-42f1-9b30-ca6bdbf51973"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"TexMo: A Multi-language Development Environment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383506","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Contemporary software systems combine many artifacts specified in various modeling and programming languages, domainspecific and general purpose as well. Since multi-language systems are so widespread, working on them calls for tools with cross-language support mechanisms such as (1) visualization, (2) static checking, (3) navigation, and (4) refactoring of cross-language relations. We investigate whether these four mechanisms indeed improve efficiency and quality of development of multi-language systems. We run a controlled experiment in which 22 participants perform typical software evolution tasks on the JTrac web application using a prototype tool implementing these mechanisms. The results speak clearly for integration of cross-language support mechanisms into software development tools, and justify research on automatic inference, manipulation and handling of cross-language relations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381762"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Code visualization","Controlled experiment","Cross language support","Domain specific languages","Multi language systems","Program comprehension","Software development tools","Software evolution","Software refactoring","Static analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cross language support mechanisms significantly aid software development","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-33666-9_12","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381762","identifier":[{"id":"84867653250","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-212ad80d-7dd6-409b-8fc1-aec4d73a2cdf"],"keyword":["Code visualization","Controlled experiment","Cross-language support","Domain-specific languages","Multi-language systems","Program comprehension","Software development tools","Software evolution","Software refactoring","Static analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-312EEF8B72422B9615F8C2E8B77BDD8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-33666-9_12","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf-Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","name_org":"Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-33666-9_12","eisbn":["9783642336669"],"isbn":["9783642336652"],"pages":"168-184","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"15th International Conference, MODELS 2012, Innsbruck, Austria, September 30–October 5, 2012. Proceedings","title":"Model Driven Engineering Languages and Systems","volume":"7590"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867653250"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-212ad80d-7dd6-409b-8fc1-aec4d73a2cdf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cross-Language Support Mechanisms Significantly Aid Software Development","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381762","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Contemporary software systems comprise many heteroge- neous artifacts; some expressed in general programming languages, some in visual and textual domain-specific languages and some in ad hoc textual formats. During construction of a system diverse artifacts are interrelated. Only few formats, typically general programming languages, provide an interface description mechanism able to specify software com- ponent boundaries. Unfortunately, these interface mechanisms can not express relations for components containing heterogeneous artifacts. We introduce Tengi, a tool that allows for the definition of software components containing heterogeneous artifacts. Tengi interfaces link components containing different textual and visual software development artifacts ranging from high-level specification documents to low-level implementation documents. We formally define and implement Tengi interfaces, a component algebra and operations on them and present a case study demonstrating Tengi’s capabilities.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383282"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Component Algebra","Domain specific languages","Heterogeneous Artifacts","Interface Description Mechanism","Software Component Boundaries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tengi interfaces for tracing between heterogeneous components","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84894148812","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383282","identifier":[{"id":"84894148812","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-89811c52-542f-4c08-96be-92027ec1ba3c"],"keyword":